City Builder (apps/city)

City simulation (engine/)
  micropolisJS, by Graeme McCutcheon and contributors: a JavaScript port of
  Micropolis, the open-source release of the 1989 city simulator by Will
  Wright and Maxis, which Don Hopkins prepared for One Laptop per Child.
  License: GNU General Public License, version 3 (engine/COPYING), with the
  additional terms in engine/LICENSE, which every copy must carry.
  Source: https://github.com/graememcc/micropolisJS, commit
  f13a1624d111d235e804bd80f48ba7c9f66a8e0f, in
  engine/micropolisJS-src.tar.gz together with frunk.store's changes
  (micropolis-web.patch, also tools/city/micropolis-web.patch in
  https://github.com/RobertPKyle/frunk-store, whose tools/build-city.mjs
  builds engine/engine.js from them).
  This is a modified version. The changes: the query tool hands its findings
  to the page instead of writing into micropolisJS's own window; each object
  keeps its own event listeners (they were shared by every object of a kind,
  so a second city, or a second plane, heard the first one's events); the
  census reads the city's own budget (it read a page element of the same
  name); and an unused import that doesn't exist is gone. Only the
  simulation, map, tools, sprites and map generator are bundled: micropolisJS's
  windows, canvas, input and jQuery are left out.
  The tile and sprite graphics (engine/tiles.png, engine/sprites.png) come
  with micropolisJS under the same terms.

